---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact" description="Prepare a website, software, automation or managed-service requirement for Blackline Development.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start a project</p>
        <h1>Start with what needs to work better.</h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">
          You do not need a finished specification before speaking to Blackline. A useful starting point is the outcome you want, what exists today, who needs to use it and anything that cannot be compromised.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="Preparing a project requirement">
        <strong>Unknowns are useful too.</strong>
        <p>
          If you know where the problem is but not the right technical answer, say that. Discovery is there to remove uncertainty before it becomes expensive implementation work.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful starting information</p>
          <h2>A short requirement is enough to begin.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The best first conversation is about the result and constraints, not a long form full of technical questions you may not be able to answer yet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">01</span>
          <h3>The outcome</h3>
          <p>What should be easier, faster, safer or possible when the work is finished?</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">02</span>
          <h3>The people</h3>
          <p>Who will use it, who owns the decision and who needs to understand the finished result?</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">03</span>
          <h3>The starting point</h3>
          <p>What already exists today — even if that is a spreadsheet, several separate tools or a manual process?</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">04</span>
          <h3>The constraints</h3>
          <p>Deadlines, integrations, budgets, privacy requirements and anything that must not change.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split-panel">
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Commissioned development</p>
        <h3>Need something built?</h3>
        <p>
          The work is scoped and priced before you choose a delivery tier, so priority changes the pace rather than quietly changing what is included.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/commissions">How commissions work</a>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Managed services</p>
        <h3>Need something kept running?</h3>
        <p>
          Hosting, maintenance, business email and domain management are available separately from commissioned development.
        </p>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/managed-services">View managed services</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
